{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\narr = [int(x) % m for x in input().split()]\n\ndef get_all_sums_modulo(subarr, mod):\n    result = {0}\n    for length in range(1, len(subarr) + 1):\n        for combo in combinations(subarr, length):\n            total = sum(combo) % mod\n            result.add(total)\n    return result\n\nhalf = n // 2\nleft_part = arr[:half]\nright_part = arr[half:]\n\nleft_sums = get_all_sums_modulo(left_part, m)\nright_sums = get_all_sums_modulo(right_part, m)\n\nright_sorted = sorted(right_sums)\nmax_sum = 0\n\nfor ls in left_sums:\n    target = m - ls\n    idx = bisect.bisect_left(right_sorted, target)\n    for j in [idx - 1, idx]:\n        if 0 <= j < len(right_sorted):\n            candidate = ls + right_sorted[j]\n            if candidate > max_sum:\n                max_sum = candidate\n\nprint(max_sum)\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] firstLine = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[0]);\n        int m = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[1]);\n        \n        String[] secondLine = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int[] arr = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            arr[i] = Integer.parseInt(secondLine[i]) % m;\n        }\n        \n        int half = n / 2;\n        int[] leftPart = new int[half];\n        int[] rightPart = new int[n - half];\n        \n        System.arraycopy(arr, 0, leftPart, 0, half);\n        System.arraycopy(arr, half, rightPart, 0, n - half);\n        \n        Set<Integer> leftSums = getAllSumsModulo(leftPart, m);\n        Set<Integer> rightSums = getAllSumsModulo(rightPart, m);\n        \n        List<Integer> rightSorted = new ArrayList<>(rightSums);\n        Collections.sort(rightSorted);\n        \n        int maxSum = 0;\n        \n        for (int ls : leftSums) {\n            int target = m - ls;\n            int idx = binarySearchLeftmost(rightSorted, target);\n            \n            for (int j : new int[]{idx - 1, idx}) {\n                if (j >= 0 && j < rightSorted.size()) {\n                    int candidate = ls + rightSorted.get(j);\n                    if (candidate > maxSum) {\n                        maxSum = candidate;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(maxSum);\n    }\n    \n    private static Set<Integer> getAllSumsModulo(int[] subarr, int mod) {\n        Set<Integer> result = new HashSet<>();\n        result.add(0);\n        \n        int n = subarr.length;\n        for (int length = 1; length <= n; length++) {\n            int[] indices = new int[length];\n            for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n                indices[i] = i;\n            }\n            \n            while (true) {\n                int total = 0;\n                for (int idx : indices) {\n                    total += subarr[idx];\n                }\n                total %= mod;\n                result.add(total);\n                \n                // Generate next combination\n                int i = length - 1;\n                while (i >= 0 && indices[i] == n - length + i) {\n                    i--;\n                }\n                \n                if (i < 0) {\n                    break;\n                }\n                \n                indices[i]++;\n                for (int j = i + 1; j < length; j++) {\n                    indices[j] = indices[j - 1] + 1;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        return result;\n    }\n    \n    private static int binarySearchLeftmost(List<Integer> list, int target) {\n        int left = 0;\n        int right = list.size();\n        \n        while (left < right) {\n            int mid = (left + right) / 2;\n            if (list.get(mid) < target) {\n                left = mid + 1;\n            } else {\n                right = mid;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        return left;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013386306818574667, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.001189835020340979, -3.3854863431770355e-05, -0.005937557201832533, -0.14284871518611908, -0.004103455226868391, -1.4662635294371285e-05, -0.00219533103518188, -0.000641974329482764, -2.884823152271565e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.00027581225731410086, -0.0021912867669016123, -0.00023529145983047783, -0.0043462105095386505, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -0.0040833912789821625, -8.237022848334163e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.13382354559144e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.005261146929115057, -0.014198003336787224, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.8412379075889476e